ELSE/crackle~.body:
[crackle~] generates noise based on a chaotic function, defined by the difference equation;
y[n] = (p + 1) * y[n-1] - y[n-2] - 0.05
inspired by SuperCollider's "Crackle" Ugen

ELSE/fbsine2~.body:
[fbsine2~] is a non-interpolating sound generator based on the difference equations below (for im = 1, fb = 0 and a = 1, a sine wave results);
x(n+1) = sin(im * y(n) + fb * x(n));
y(n+1) = (a * y(n) + c) % 2pi

ELSE/ikeda~.body:
[ikeda~] is an ikeda map chaotic generator with two audio outputs, generated by the difference equations;
y1[n] = 1 + u * (y1[n-1] * cos(t) - y2[n-1] * sin(t));
y2[n] = u * (y1[n-1] * sin(t) + y2[n-1] * cos(t));
where t = 0.4 - 6 / (1 + y1[n-1]^2 + y2[n-1]^2)

ELSE/latoocarfian~.body:
[latoocarfian~] is a chaotic generator using the difference equations;
x[n] = sin(a * y[n-1]) + d * sin(a * x[n-1]);
y[n] = sin(b * x[n]) + c * sin(b * y[n-1]);

ELSE/standard~.body:
This object was based on SuperCollider's "StandardN" UGEN;
The standard map is an area preserving map of a cylinder discovered by the plasma physicist Boris Chirikov.

[standard~] is a standard map chaotic generator. The sound is generated with the difference equations;
y[n] = (y[n-1] + k * sin(x[n-1])) % 2pi;
x[n] = (x[n-1] + y[n]) % 2pi;
out = (x[n] - pi) / pi;
The output rate of the equation is given in Hz (default: Nyquist).
